00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
first up avalanche has delivered on a  big time request for hogwarts legacy by  giving fans the ability to link their  wizarding world fan club accounts  formerly known as pottermore to their wb  account for hogwarts legacy this will  bring over both the wand and hogwarts  house that was given to players on the  wizarding world website the fan site  also has a patronus quiz however  avalanche didn't mention whether or not  the patronus would transfer into the  game along with the wand and house at  number two in addition to the account  link announcement avalanche also  revealed special bonuses that will be  granted to players who choose to link  their accounts in the form of these  house fanatic robes as well as this big  skull mask even better the robes will  always match the house you're currently  playing on which is great for players  who are planning on multiple  playthroughs avalanche also confirmed  you can link your account to get the  rewards and still choose not to bring  over your house or wand this is mainly  for players who prefer a different house  or wand than the one they've been given  on the wizarding world website and by  the way guys if you're one of those  people who isn't happy with your result  you can always delete your wizarding  world account sign up again using the  exact same email and retake the quizzes  i would just make sure you do all of  that before you link it to the wb  account for number three with all of the  recent trailers it would be easy to  forget some of the smaller updates  avalanche has given starting with an  updated faq they officially confirmed no  playable quidditch which we reported on  here back in july the updated faq also  has an interesting answer regarding  morality in hogwarts legacy it states  hogwarts legacy does not have a morality  system but players will encounter  various quests and storylines that will  influence the witch or wizard they  choose to become considering we already  know we'll have an opportunity to decide  between at least a few different choices  throughout missions this update has left  me with more questions than answers do  they simply mean there's no system that  tracks our morality and choices as in  you won't forge a completely new path  whether you choose to play completely  good or completely evil or does it mean  our choices won't matter at all i find  the latter hard to believe considering  the reveal trailer said this the choices  you make now  will define the legacy  of the conference  and there's also an additional faq post  that states players will also encounter  quests and scenarios that will pose  difficult choices and determine what  they stand for i mean what's the point  in standing for something if it has no  impact at all on the story quest please  let it actually have an impact on the  story speaking of quests as we move on  to number four here the trailer showing  off sebastian's sallow's quest line was  confirmed by community manager chandler  wood to be an entirely optional quest  and then in a recent playstation blog  post wood also confirmed optional quest  lines for both natsionai and poppy  sweeting the gryffindor and hufflepuff  companion respectively those are the  only three companions that have been  revealed so far which has fans  desperately wanting to know is there a  ravenclaw companion and if so why  haven't we found out about them yet  number five in a recent sony state of  play we got a new trailer for the  haunted hogsmeade shop quest line yet  another optional quest in hogwarts  legacy unfortunately for pc xbox and  switch players this quest is a timed  exclusive on playstation platforms for a  full calendar year i suppose on the  bright side at least we found out that  it's only a timed quest and not a fully  exclusive quest to playstation for  playstation gamers you should know this  does not require a pre-order or a  specific version of the game if you're  playing on the playstation platform  you'll have access to this quest now  this is just me here but i would assume  this will eventually be released to all  players in february 2024 but it hasn't  been confirmed yet just how avalanche  will handle a possible rollout to the  other platforms once that exclusivity  with sony runs out as for number six  while the quest doesn't require  pre-ordering wb and playstation are  offering a pre-order bonus to entice  players and it comes in the form of a  felix felicis potion recipe according to  wood in a playstation blog post the  liquid luck potion will reveal gear  chests on the minimap for one in-game  day but it is just the recipe players  will still need to brew the potion with  help from their potions lessons and the  potions stations in the room of  requirement oh and by the way yes would  also just confirm that hogwarts legacy  will have a map as well as day night  cycles something we were already pretty  sure was going to be in but nice to have  it confirmed here number seven the  haunted hogsmeade shop trailer also  introduced us to three new characters  the first being cassandra mason a name  that was leaked two years ago on actress  julia farino's imdb page farino is also  set to voice a character by the name of  helen thistlewood who seems a likely  candidate for the herbology professor as  for the other two characters in the  trailer we only hear their voices but if  you watch playstation's version of the  trailer with the captions turned on  you'll see their names revealed as penny  and fast studio penny sounds like a  small girl or more likely a house elf  considering she refers to madame mason  as her mistress she has had rotten bad  luck with the last few tenants  fastidio on the other hand sounds like a  malevolent being and considering that  the shop is haunted many fans have  guessed he could be a poltergeist to his  taken up residence in the shop those who  came before you just could not seem to  escape the darkness  now for number eight with the haunted  hogsbeat shop trailer avalanche also  revealed yet another in-game costume in  the form of the shopkeeper's cosmetic  set completing the haunted hogsmeade  quest will reward players with this set  in addition to a shop of their own where  they can sell items and gear at better  rates than anywhere else unfortunately  it also seems this shop is only for  playstation and the official hogwarts  legacy twitter account actually  responded to a question with the  following answer completion of the  haunted hogsmeade shop quest is the only  way to receive an in-game hogsmeade shop  to own the quest is exclusive to  playstation consoles through february  10th 2024. now just my own little  interjection here i think it's really  interesting wording here because of the  fact that they say sell items and gear  at better rates than anywhere else to me  that implies that other players will at  least have somewhere to sell the items  and gear that we have it just won't be  in the form of this dedicated shop that  we own in hogsmeade and really until  someone outside of avalanche wb or  playstation is able to actually see this  and play through this and comment on it  then we really aren't going to know just  how significant of a detail this  actually is i mean it could be a very  small minor thing or it could actually  be a significant thing in terms of  owning our own shop i mean is this some  sort of passive thing that just kind of  happens in the background once you have  the shop unlocked or will it have more  active things that you will have to  physically go into the shop to do in  order to sell these items at number nine  there have been two hogwarts legacy  books listed on amazon for quite some  time the art and making of hogwarts  legacy from inside editions as well as  hogwarts legacy the official game guide  the latter recently saw an update with a  full cover reveal for the first time the  artwork is similar to the box art of the  standard edition of the game however it  features a different student and also a  character holding their wand in their  left hand i'm pretty sure this marks the  first time we've seen a character in  hogwarts legacy with a wand in their  left hand and this now has some fans  wondering is this confirmation that  lefties will be able to play the game  with their dominant hand as their wand  arm now as much as i would like to say  yes i certainly would not take this  cover art as confirmation of that  considering that artists can take  creative liberties to make something  that will look the best and may not  necessarily be 100 accurate to the game  and depending on code and even the level  design and enemy design of the game  sometimes these things can be very  simple to just flip and have the  character use their other hand but then  there are other times that it's way more  difficult than you would imagine i  remember it was a huge deal with the  legend of zelda twilight princess which  was a gamecube game originally but then  also launched on the nintendo wii well  in the wii version link was right-handed  because nintendo had the wii remote and  knew that most people were right-handed  whereas in the gamecube version link was  still left-handed but what's really  interesting about that is that the games  had to be complete mirrors of one  another so rather than everything being  exactly the same the world was  essentially completely flipped or  mirrored in the wii version with link  now using the sword in his right hand  now avalanche has also released four  glorious trailers all in 4k resolution  showcasing the four hogwarts common  rooms we'd seen each room briefly before  but these trailers give us our best look  so far at all of the incredible detail  avalanche is including here ravenclaw  features an orderly bright common room  with plenty of spots for studying  gryffindor is a welcoming and  comfortable space that shows off school  spirit house pride and a remembrance of  former gryffindors with numerous  portraits hufflepuff has nailed that  warm earthy feel with plenty of areas  that encourage social interaction and  numerous plants that help bring life to  the space and while slytherin may be in  the dungeons the vast windows looking  out into the black lake let plenty of  light filter through you'll find bizarre  relics strange items and what has to be  the most jaw-dropping entrance of all  four with the slytherin common room and  all four of these common rooms have so  many amazing details and tiny little  secrets for you to find i've actually  done full breakdown videos of each  hogwarts house common room so take a  look at the videos on your screen now  and jump straight to my breakdowns of  your favorite hogwarts house as always  thank you all so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon

